    "result": "Done! I've fixed the floating point precision bug in three functions that convert prices to cents:\n\n**Changes made:**\n- `src/money.js` (line 13): Wrapped `parseEuros()` conversion with `Math.round()`\n- `src/money.js` (line 25): Wrapped `cellCents()` conversion with `Math.round()`\n- `src/locale.js` (line 18): Wrapped `decimalCommaToCents()` conversion with `Math.round()`\n\n**Why it happened:** When JavaScript multiplies `39.95 * 100`, floating point arithmetic produces `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`. The validation requires an integer, so it rejected it even though the math was essentially correct.\n\n**Testing confirmed:** All three subscriptions (Gym 39.95, Netflix 12.99, Spotify 10.99) now add successfully.",
